WEBVTT

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:40.980
It's the fairyland at the bottom of the universe.

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:43.050
Dreams in a wasteland.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:45.310
A town overrun with violence.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:47.480
The idiot's utopia.

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:52.030
The planet people call "Endless Illusion."

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.620
A man named Van...

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:57.450
who operates the strongest Armor.

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:00.410
A girl named Wendy...

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:02.660
who's searching for her abducted brother.

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:06.170
Two travelers guided by the mark of the Claw.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:08.380
Who will they encounter at the bottom of the wound?

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:11.670
A noble enemy, or a filthy ally?

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:15.960
Twin's Guards

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:20.350
Could we have lost our way?

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:22.980
No one could be stupid enough to get lost on a straight path like this.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:24.350
That's not what I mean.

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:26.150
I'm wondering whether it was a mistake...

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:27.230
to come into this valley!

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:30.570
If we keep moving forward, we'll come out somewhere.

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:32.490
If you've got a problem with that, go back yourself.

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:35.110
Good grief! You're sounding like a child.

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:41.700
A town?

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:42.830
Looks that way.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.500
What is this place?

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:50.750
I've never seen anything like it.

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:57.300
Is this a town?

00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:58.640
I don't know.

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:01.180
I wonder if anyone's here.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:02.100
Don't know.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:06.980
What's that?

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:14.440
Even the hounds killed each other at the same time.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:17.410
How annoying!

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:19.910
They're the same person?

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:22.200
You should be thankful, shouldn't you?

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:24.250
If it wasn't for that, your head would have been...

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:25.660
rolling around on the ground a long time ago.

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:26.870
Thankful for what?

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:30.210
You're the one who's always groveling across the floor.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:35.470
Who are you?

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:37.630
The bodyguard that woman told us about?

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:38.890
That woman?

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:40.050
Don't look at me.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:46.810
All right everyone. Stop right there.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:50.440
Oh! It must be...

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:51.310
Ms. Carul!

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:53.150
Carmen99.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:55.150
Ms. Carmen.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.070
I was looking all over for you.

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:01.410
I never imagined you'd be getting here before me.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:05.370
So then I take it, he's the bodyguard.

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:08.870
Yes. I'll bring the contract later.

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:09.920
What about the other one?

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:12.710
Don't worry. I've already found someone.

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:16.420
So both of you, please be patient.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:18.800
And please see to it that I'm paid.

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:22.850
It sure is a strange town.

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:23.850
Yes, it is.

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:26.430
But what's even more surprising is the fact...

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:28.770
you haven't run away from Van yet.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:30.810
I'm the one who wants to run away.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:34.860
Carmen, why does everyone in this town...

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:37.070
look the same as someone else?

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:39.240
Oh, that? They say they're all twins.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:40.950
All of them?

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:42.910
Although there aren't many of them left.

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:44.790
They divided themselves between left and right, and...

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:46.200
have been fighting for a long time now.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:48.160
Like the two dogs earlier?

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:50.830
Right. It always ends up with killing each other at the same time.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:54.460
They say twins have special bond, which makes it all the more ironic.

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:58.630
Why would they do that when they're sisters?

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:00.470
According to the father's will...

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:03.300
the one who wins out can have the inheritance all to herself.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:04.810
It's located in a building in back.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:07.930
Did you see the pendants the two of them had on?

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:11.190
When combined together it's said they become the key to the entrance.

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:12.730
What's the inheritance?

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:14.820
From what I understand, even they don't know.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:16.860
He sure was an irresponsible father, wasn't he?

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:18.860
In that case, shouldn't they make peace and...

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:20.150
divide it up amongst everyone?

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:24.870
Given the people who've been lost, and the mutual hatred...

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:27.790
that way of solving things no longer exists.

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:29.410
That's terrible.

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:32.000
You're after the inheritance?

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:33.170
Don't be ridiculous.

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:36.920
In exchange for finding bodyguards for both of them...

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:39.800
I'll be receiving the loser's fortune from the winner.

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:42.720
So, Van, it's a bit last second but...

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:45.850
will you be a bodyguard and duel on behalf of one of them?

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:46.760
What?

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:49.020
The pay's not too bad either.

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:52.350
Earl Driver. Nice to meet you.

00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:56.110
I'd like all the condiments you got.

00:05:56.650 --> 00:05:57.110
Hey.

00:05:57.110 --> 00:05:57.770
Certainly.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:00.740
Tell us whatever you want. You don't have to hold back.

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:03.240
There's one thing I'd like to ask.

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:05.910
You really think you can settle this thing...

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:08.120
by having other people fight it out for you?

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:10.830
We can't lose any more of our people.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:13.500
And the other side is willing to accept the outcome?

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:15.330
We'll make them.

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:19.460
And if I lose, you can accept it?

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:20.460
Van!

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:21.510
I don't know.

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:23.090
But you don't want to die, do you?

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:25.970
No. I fully expect to be paid for my services.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:27.760
You want information, don't you?

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:30.270
About the Claw.

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:36.270
He used to come see my Papa once in a while, a long time ago.

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:38.900
They were always having long passionate discussions.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:41.860
He was a kind person.

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:43.780
I liked him second only to Papa.

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:46.110
You have information?

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:47.570
We probably have something at the family home.

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:49.450
So when do I do my thing?

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:52.000
Not until Elle decides on her bodyguard.

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:54.830
We want you to protect Earl until then.

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:57.460
Carmen will fill you in on the details.

00:06:57.790 --> 00:06:58.630
I see.

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:00.670
Which side is she on?

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:03.300
She's on her own side.

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:06.930
You shouldn't have to wait long.

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:09.300
She said it would be 2 or 3 days at the most.

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:12.430
In the meantime, we've prepared a room for you here.

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:15.560
Who are you?

00:07:29.450 --> 00:07:30.740
What are you doing?

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:32.120
I'm the bodyguard.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:34.960
Viest!

00:07:39.170 --> 00:07:40.090
Hey!

00:07:40.090 --> 00:07:42.170
You're not supposed to take things into your own hands!

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:56.020
Someone! Prepare the emergency room!

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:57.270
Viest has been shot!

00:07:57.640 --> 00:07:59.350
Viest? All right.

00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:00.860
I'll send some people over there too.

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:03.780
Hey! Who's that guy?

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:05.940
He's the bodyguard for the other side.

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:08.820
He took off right after I told him about it.

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:14.160
I just met him too, but he's a drifter like you...

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:16.290
and probably has about the same level of ability.

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:18.250
His name is Ray.

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:20.710
Ray Lundgren. But...

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:26.510
I can't agree to this. It's just more of the same thing.

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:27.880
Really?

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:30.680
One of theirs was injured but you're not.

00:08:30.930 --> 00:08:31.640
Well, yes.

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:34.390
This town has finally changed.

00:08:34.970 --> 00:08:37.850
I've stared at my own face long enough.

00:08:40.230 --> 00:08:44.230
Now, now. Why can't you two get along?

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:48.700
Be nice to each other, be nice you two.

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:51.570
I'm sorry Papa.

00:08:52.570 --> 00:08:55.540
But I can't have you all to myself if I do that.

00:08:56.620 --> 00:09:00.460
Why? Why am I the only one who can't leave here?

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:02.580
It's to keep you from getting mixed up in this.

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:03.170
Carmen.

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:04.170
Yeah.

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:06.050
You're in charge of looking after her.

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:08.340
Stay here until you come watch over the proceedings tomorrow.

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:10.130
Guess I don't have much choice.

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:18.560
If our bodyguard tries to get out of fighting his opponent, then...

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:19.930
Yes. I know what to do.

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:22.850
Damn. I wasn't counting on this.

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:26.320
I didn't think Ray would be such a lunatic.

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:28.570
Sorry for getting you caught up in this.

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:29.820
It doesn't make sense.

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:31.990
Why are they all killing each other?

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:40.410
Good evening, everyone!

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:42.290
Is Ray here?

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:51.130
Stop!

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:52.260
Please stop!

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:54.970
Hey, listen.

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:59.970
I was given a job. I was told to protect someone.

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:03.850
And so I've come to kill you...

00:10:05.690 --> 00:10:07.770
before you kill the person who hired me.

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:20.330
Somebody! We have an intruder!

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:21.660
Come quick! Somebody!

00:10:28.170 --> 00:10:30.550
I want to go to another town soon.

00:10:34.470 --> 00:10:35.760
Carmen.

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:37.220
What is it?

00:10:40.270 --> 00:10:41.720
Who's Elena?

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:44.690
Who told you about Elena?

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:47.400
Van did. He was talking in his sleep.

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:50.780
Is she a woman?

00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:53.990
Is there some connection between her and the Claw?

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:10.460
Don't move.

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:13.510
This is where we settle it.

00:11:14.090 --> 00:11:15.880
I don't know how much they're paying you...

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:17.340
but you got a raw deal.

00:11:17.590 --> 00:11:19.720
Money only dulls the spirit.

00:11:20.390 --> 00:11:22.680
In my world there's no need for that sort of thing.

00:11:23.930 --> 00:11:26.230
There's only one thing I want.

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:28.020
Death.

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:30.820
The Claw's death.

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:33.940
He killed my wife.

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:38.110
And so I'm going to find and kill him.

00:11:38.700 --> 00:11:39.530
You're...

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:43.620
Elena was the woman Van was going to marry.

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:46.330
What? Was she kidnapped too?

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:49.960
No. On her wedding day...

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:52.590
Elena was killed...

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:54.170
by the Claw.

00:11:56.260 --> 00:11:58.550
I see. You too.

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:02.350
But I'm the one who's going to kill him.

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:04.220
You're not up for the task.

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:09.310
Could you stand back and watch her die?

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:13.360
Why? Why did you have those two meet each other?

00:12:13.610 --> 00:12:15.320
Because that's my job.

00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:19.030
Their journey is a journey of revenge.

00:12:19.030 --> 00:12:21.820
It's not a pretty thing. They're risking their lives.

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:24.740
They need to be prepared for that sort of thing.

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:29.670
I use them and they use me.

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:33.170
It's not easy getting your hands on information.

00:12:33.170 --> 00:12:34.000
But...

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:37.300
If you don't like what you see then go back home, pipsqueak.

00:12:37.300 --> 00:12:39.630
'Cause there's no telling when it's gonna be his turn to die.

00:12:39.630 --> 00:12:40.890
I'm fully prepared!

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:44.100
I'm on my own journey.

00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:46.020
I've decided to help my brother.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:49.440
And don't compare Van with that man!

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:49.980
Van is...

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:51.060
Yeah, yeah.

00:12:51.940 --> 00:12:54.020
Just as I thought, you can't do anything, can you?

00:12:55.530 --> 00:12:57.490
In that case, how about this...

00:12:57.990 --> 00:13:00.490
I'll betray them and come over to your side.

00:13:00.820 --> 00:13:02.620
You're gonna betray the person who hired you?

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:04.580
After all, we have the same objective.

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:07.540
So we should try and maximize our chances for success.

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:10.750
What do you think?

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:11.920
Are you game?

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:16.880
No. I'd be dishonoring Elena...

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:19.590
if I joined up with someone who's strayed from the path like you.

00:13:20.970 --> 00:13:23.300
You think you can live according to your code...

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:24.260
while seeking vengeance?

00:13:25.350 --> 00:13:27.520
In that case, we'll settle things tomorrow.

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:28.060
Yeah.

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:29.810
You...

00:13:31.270 --> 00:13:32.940
Your vengeance is...

00:13:33.610 --> 00:13:35.230
very kind.

00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:44.950
Elle! Papa's inheritance is mine.

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:49.080
Starting today, that face and voice of yours will be mine alone.

00:13:49.910 --> 00:13:51.790
Acting as the witness, I now confirm the following.

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:54.540
Both teams will abide by the outcome of the fight...

00:13:54.540 --> 00:13:57.050
with the losing side handing over the key and...

00:13:57.050 --> 00:13:59.510
submitting unconditionally to the winner's demands. OK?

00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:04.300
Well then, you two move over to the dueling area...

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:05.390
located by the entrance.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:11.310
Earl!

00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:13.060
You!

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:21.150
Stop!

00:14:23.450 --> 00:14:24.490
The key is complete!

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:27.030
Elle!

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.710
Ost! Watch out!

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:53.560
I wonder what's inside.

00:14:56.650 --> 00:14:59.690
Please take me...

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:02.570
to where my father is.

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:12.120
An Armor?

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:15.420
You must be joking.

00:15:15.420 --> 00:15:17.080
There must be something I can take as a reward.

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:21.880
This is Papa's inheritance?

00:15:22.090 --> 00:15:23.760
Who cares about your stupid inheritance?

00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:25.260
Where's the clue that will lead me to the Claw?

00:15:25.930 --> 00:15:27.050
Where is it?

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:29.640
And don't tell me you don't have anything either.

00:15:29.930 --> 00:15:30.390
Damn you.

00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:36.230
It's too late now, Earl.

00:15:36.850 --> 00:15:38.480
Papa's inheritance is mine.

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:39.730
Now be a good sport and give up.

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:40.440
Comrade!

00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:43.690
Papa.

00:15:45.990 --> 00:15:48.160
We have, for the most part, seen the completion...

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:50.280
of the Armor that you asked for, Twin Lock.

00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:53.660
We had hoped to use the ability clones have...

00:15:53.660 --> 00:15:56.410
to empathize with each other to boost its functionality. However...

00:15:56.660 --> 00:15:58.290
What does he mean, "clone"?

00:15:58.290 --> 00:15:59.040
I don't know.

00:15:59.710 --> 00:16:01.130
I am terribly sorry.

00:16:01.630 --> 00:16:04.920
The specialized pilot training was a complete and total failure.

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:09.220
And due to the outbreak of a pathogen during the research process...

00:16:09.220 --> 00:16:12.050
we will most likely perish before you come here.

00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:17.440
I hope that at least you got the data for the Carossa Project.

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:21.360
The Armor must be designed for two people.

00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:27.030
The experimental bodies in the town in the valley are all samples...

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:28.200
for us to collect data.

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:31.410
We manipulated the emotions for our objective...

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:34.660
as a result of our technical insufficiency.

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:39.500
If they're rude to you, please feel free to dispose of them.

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:43.750
I can not tell you enough how sorry I am.

00:16:44.550 --> 00:16:49.430
But even now, our love for you is infinite.

00:16:49.430 --> 00:16:54.180
Even if the promise is no longer valid, and you've given up on us...

00:16:54.930 --> 00:16:57.430
For your sake, I...

00:17:00.390 --> 00:17:01.900
You came all this way for nothing.

00:17:05.650 --> 00:17:06.480
Papa...

00:17:09.610 --> 00:17:10.110
Hey!

00:17:10.990 --> 00:17:12.660
That was a lie just now, wasn't it?

00:17:12.950 --> 00:17:16.330
The stuff Papa said about us being samples, and disposing of us.

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:17.750
Let go.

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:18.700
Elle!

00:17:19.710 --> 00:17:20.410
You bastard!

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:40.520
You're no longer a person.

00:17:40.730 --> 00:17:41.850
Yeah, that's right.

00:17:42.190 --> 00:17:45.400
Being human only gets in the way, when you're out for revenge.

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:50.700
I can't stand you.

00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:52.030
The feeling's mutual.

00:17:52.240 --> 00:17:54.240
I hate you too. But...

00:17:56.410 --> 00:18:00.040
Now, now. Why can't you two get along.

00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:02.830
We should have listened to what he said.

00:18:03.370 --> 00:18:04.710
If we'd done that, then Papa...

00:18:05.630 --> 00:18:07.920
No, there's still time.

00:18:10.970 --> 00:18:12.050
Together, the two of us.

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:15.050
Let's meet Papa's expectations.

00:18:20.810 --> 00:18:22.520
It's the least they could do.

00:18:22.730 --> 00:18:25.940
Detect the signal. Start twin maneuver.

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:29.980
Turbo... Separate the first control.

00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:31.360
Adjust the...

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:34.700
Papa!

00:18:38.030 --> 00:18:39.200
They're in the Armor?

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:46.460
It's Papa, Elle! We're inside of Papa!

00:18:46.460 --> 00:18:48.340
I know. I can feel it.

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:50.460
Papa is ours!

00:18:50.760 --> 00:18:52.720
We're not handing him over to anyone!

00:18:52.720 --> 00:18:53.420
No!

00:18:53.760 --> 00:18:55.760
This place is ours alone!

00:19:01.390 --> 00:19:02.600
I don't have any choice.

00:19:20.910 --> 00:19:21.660
An Armor?

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:23.500
Wake up, Dann.

00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:26.420
Get out of that thing!

00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:27.880
We're...

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:29.340
together with Papa!

00:19:34.720 --> 00:19:36.720
Come quick! We're getting out of here!

00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:37.890
But what about Van?

00:19:38.260 --> 00:19:39.550
He'll be fine.

00:19:39.550 --> 00:19:41.930
You want to continue your journey, don't you?

00:19:45.230 --> 00:19:47.730
Get out of that thing! Why are you fighting?

00:19:48.060 --> 00:19:49.860
It's what Papa wants!

00:19:50.020 --> 00:19:51.690
Now we're with Papa.

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:53.570
The three of us are all living happily together.

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:54.320
That's why.

00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:56.110
You're in the way too!

00:19:58.820 --> 00:20:00.320
This place is a graveyard.

00:20:00.620 --> 00:20:01.660
We're together with Papa.

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:02.830
Always together!

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:04.620
Wherever together!

00:20:06.210 --> 00:20:08.870
I see. In that case, here's what I'll do.

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:22.850
Sanctions Charge, Volcain.

00:20:26.810 --> 00:20:28.560
He's got Armor too!

00:20:34.780 --> 00:20:35.780
Papa!

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:40.820
Papa, don't abandon us!

00:20:41.490 --> 00:20:44.120
We can even dance well.

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:46.120
Delete.

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:48.460
Stop it!

00:20:49.420 --> 00:20:51.040
Ray, you're going too far!

00:20:51.040 --> 00:20:53.090
Get off your high horse. There's no point in being kind!

00:20:57.630 --> 00:21:00.220
Papa, our dance.

00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:07.600
There's something I need to do.

00:21:07.980 --> 00:21:09.100
And in order to do it...

00:21:10.310 --> 00:21:11.600
I will never hesitate!

00:21:16.070 --> 00:21:19.740
I will remove anything which stands in the way of my purpose.

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:21.740
No matter what it is.

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:25.200
Elle.

00:21:25.620 --> 00:21:26.370
Earl.

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:30.000
The two of us.

00:21:30.660 --> 00:21:31.460
Why?

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:41.050
Ray!

00:21:43.510 --> 00:21:44.300
Ray!

00:21:44.890 --> 00:21:45.970
Ray!

00:22:01.400 --> 00:22:01.990
Van!

00:22:02.360 --> 00:22:04.370
What happened to everyone?

00:22:05.530 --> 00:22:08.290
Well, I'll see you around if you're still alive.

00:22:10.870 --> 00:22:12.750
That job left a bad taste in my mouth.

00:22:18.550 --> 00:22:19.550
It can't be.

00:23:53.140 --> 00:23:54.480
Light My Fire

00:23:54.480 --> 00:23:58.020
You really never know what's going to happen when you're on a journey.
Light My Fire

00:23:58.020 --> 00:23:58.850
Light My Fire

00:23:58.850 --> 00:24:01.770
The place was refreshing, a peaceful port town.
Light My Fire

00:24:01.770 --> 00:24:02.780
Light My Fire

00:24:02.780 --> 00:24:05.650
But even there, Van's life was in danger.
Light My Fire

00:24:05.650 --> 00:24:06.490
Light My Fire

00:24:06.490 --> 00:24:09.660
Blue sky, white clouds, Van running around.
Light My Fire

00:24:09.660 --> 00:24:10.240
Light My Fire

00:24:10.240 --> 00:24:12.160
Before we knew it, the town was in an uproar.
Light My Fire

00:24:12.160 --> 00:24:13.990
A complete waste of a tropical paradise.
Light My Fire

00:24:13.990 --> 00:24:14.910
Light My Fire

00:24:14.910 --> 00:24:19.020
And it was the place where our journey took a major turn.
